      "alt": "System architecture diagram illustrating a multimodal transformer model split into \"UNDERSTANDING\" and \"GENERATION\" sections alongside a \"State (the KV cache)\" column.\n * State (the KV cache): A vertical stack of cached key-value tokens ordered from bottom to top: text:0, text:1, image:0, text:2, text:3, text:4, text:5, and video:0.\n * Understanding Pipeline: Starts with a \"Text\" box displaying video metadata (<|metadata|>, 384×672, 24 fps, frames 0-127, anchor image:0, <|content_media|>). This feeds into a \"Text head\" consisting of blue transformer blocks (Block 1 through Block N) handling \"Text\" and \"Visual\" inputs.\n * Generation Pipeline: Features a \"Diffusion head\" consisting of orange transformer blocks (Block 1 through Block N, denoted with a ×8 repeat count). Each block in the Diffusion head connects to its corresponding block in the Text head via horizontal dashed lines labeled \"shared attention\".\n * Data Flow: \"Noisy latents\" enter at the bottom of the Diffusion head, and outputs flow upward to a \"Decoder\", which updates the KV cache with \"video:0 written to the state\".\n",
